IMPORT prelude

-- Hazardous Waste (Control of Export, Import and Transit) Act 1997 (Singapore) -- what counts as hazardous or other waste (ss 4, 5,
-- 9, 10, Annex II of the Schedule), what a transit proposal is (s 6), the military exemption (s 12), the bars on granting a permit
-- (ss 22, 23), the prohibitions on importing, exporting and transiting waste and their penalties (ss 25 to 27), entry into a
-- dwelling (s 31(2)), the enforcement offences and their penalties (ss 29, 30, 32 to 37), officers of a company (s 42) and the appeal
-- against a refusal of a permit (s 45).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 January 2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/HWCEITA1997.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December
-- 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the deposit is S 871/2024 wef 01/01/2025, which amends the Basel Convention annexes in
-- the Schedule (including Annex II, which now ends with entry Y49, electrical and electronic waste).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0082 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the classification of waste, the three prohibitions and the offences a trader, carrier or company officer
-- meets. Not encoded: the regulation-making provisions (ss 17 to 20, 48) beyond the penalty ceiling in s 48(2)(e), the
-- corresponding-requirement rules between sets of Article 11 regulations (s 21), the fee rule (s 24), the time limit for permit
-- conditions (s 11), injunctions (s 28), the content of the movement-control and search powers (ss 30 to 32), evidentiary
-- certificates (ss 39 to 41), service (s 46), Convention countries (s 47), and the Basel Convention text in the Schedule except the
-- headings of Annexes I to III. No regulations made under the Act were retrieved, so "prescribed" waste and every permit condition are
-- inputs.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Hazardous Waste (Control of Export, Import and Transit) Act 1997 -- waste and movements`

DECLARE Movement IS ONE OF
    `import`
    `export`
    `transit`

-- s 2(1): "waste" means a substance or object that is "(a) proposed to be disposed of; (b) disposed of; or (c) required by any
-- written law to be disposed of". The Annex flags below stand for membership of a category or characteristic in the Basel
-- Convention as set out in the Schedule; which category a real substance falls in is not encoded.
DECLARE Waste HAS
    `is waste within s 2` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in an Annex I category` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an Annex III characteristic` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in an Annex II category` IS A BOOLEAN
    `from the normal operations of a ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `radioactive` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The other country is the country of export (for an import) or of destination (for an export or a transit).
DECLARE Country HAS
    `party to the Basel Convention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `listed on the Secretariat website as classifying it hazardous` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has declared it hazardous for that country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `party to an Article 11 arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangement controls it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangement expressly excludes it` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `4 -- hazardous waste and other waste`

-- s 4: "Subject to section 5", (a) "hazardous waste" means (i) "waste prescribed by any regulations made under this Act, where the
-- waste has any of the characteristics mentioned in Annex III", or (ii) waste in any category in Annex I "unless it does not possess
-- any of the characteristics contained in Annex III"; (b) "other waste" means waste in any category in Annex II (Y46 "Wastes
-- collected from households", Y47 incineration residues of household wastes, Y48 plastic waste with exceptions, Y49 electrical and
-- electronic waste); "but hazardous and other wastes do not include wastes which derive from the normal operations of a ship and
-- radioactive wastes".
--
-- Both limbs of (a) need an Annex III characteristic: prescribing a waste by regulation does not make it hazardous without one.
GIVEN `the waste` IS A Waste
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is hazardous or other waste under s 4` IF
        `the waste`'s `is waste within s 2`
    AND (NOT `the waste`'s `from the normal operations of a ship`)
    AND (NOT `the waste`'s `radioactive`)
    AND (    (`the waste`'s `prescribed by regulations` AND `the waste`'s `has an Annex III characteristic`)
         OR  (`the waste`'s `in an Annex I category` AND `the waste`'s `has an Annex III characteristic`)
         OR  `the waste`'s `in an Annex II category`)

§§ `5, 9 and 10 -- the extended and the excluded meaning`

-- s 5(1): applies only to an export, or a transit "that involves the taking out of Singapore of a substance or object to a particular
-- foreign country". (2): if the country is a Basel party and the prescribed website of the Secretariat states that the substance is,
-- in particular circumstances, classified as hazardous or other waste under its law, then it is hazardous or other waste "for those
-- purposes". (3), (4), (5): a Minister's declaration in the Gazette (for a Basel party's classification, or for household waste the
-- country classifies as hazardous) "has effect accordingly".
-- s 9(2): if the country is a party to an Article 11 arrangement and the substance is "subject to notification or control under the
-- arrangement", it is "taken to be hazardous or other waste" -- for an import, an export or a transit.
-- s 10(2): if the arrangement "expressly provides that the substance or object is not subject to notification or control", it is
-- "taken not to be hazardous or other waste".
--
-- INFERENCES (the text does not rank them): s 10 is applied last and overrides everything, because it has no "apart from this
-- section" qualifier; s 5 and s 9 are applied without the s 2 meaning of waste or the ship and radioactive exclusions in s 4,
-- because s 4 is "subject to section 5" and s 9 speaks of a "substance or object".
GIVEN `the waste` IS A Waste, `the movement` IS A Movement, `the other country` IS A Country
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is hazardous or other waste` IF
        (NOT (`the other country`'s `party to an Article 11 arrangement` AND `the other country`'s `the arrangement expressly excludes it`))
    AND (    `is hazardous or other waste under s 4` `the waste`
         OR  (`the other country`'s `party to an Article 11 arrangement` AND `the other country`'s `the arrangement controls it`)
         OR  (    (NOT (`the movement` EQUALS `import`))
              AND (    (`the other country`'s `party to the Basel Convention` AND `the other country`'s `listed on the Secretariat website as classifying it hazardous`)
                   OR  `the other country`'s `the Minister has declared it hazardous for that country`)))

§§ `6 -- transit proposals`

-- s 6(2): a proposal "(a) to bring hazardous or other waste into Singapore for the purpose of being carried to a foreign country
-- either by the same or another conveyance; and (b) if the waste is brought into Singapore by sea or air, the carriage is on a through
-- bill of lading or through airway bill, is a transit proposal so long as it is not proposed to dispose of the waste in Singapore".
-- s 2(1): a through bill is one "from a place outside Singapore to a final destination outside Singapore without a consignee in
-- Singapore". Waste brought in by land needs no through bill.
GIVEN `bound for a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN, `brought in by sea or air` IS A BOOLEAN, `on a through bill` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disposal in Singapore is proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a transit proposal` IF
        `bound for a foreign country`
    AND ((NOT `brought in by sea or air`) OR `on a through bill`)
    AND (NOT `disposal in Singapore is proposed`)

§§ `22 and 23 -- when the Director-General must not grant a permit`

-- s 23: the Director-General "must not grant a Basel permit or special permit if he or she is satisfied that the grant could result in
-- hazardous or other waste being brought into Antarctica" (s 2(1): south of 60 degrees South latitude).
-- s 22(1), (3), (5): where a proposal for a Basel permit is within the scope of a set of Article 11 regulations, the Director-General
-- "must not grant the permit unless he or she is satisfied that the corresponding requirements of that set of regulations have been
-- met". These are bars only: the Act does not say when a permit must be granted.
GIVEN `could result in waste reaching Antarctica` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the scope of a set of Article 11 regulations` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `corresponding requirements met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant is barred` IF
        `could result in waste reaching Antarctica`
    OR  (`within the scope of a set of Article 11 regulations` AND (NOT `corresponding requirements met`))

§§ `12, 25, 26 and 27 -- the three prohibitions`

-- s 25(1): a person must not import hazardous or other waste unless "(a) the person is the holder of an import permit ...; (b) the
-- import is authorised by an order made under any regulation made under Part 3; or (c) the import has been ordered under any
-- regulation made under Part 3". (2): the holder must not import "except in accordance with the permit" or, "whether before or after
-- importing", breach any permit condition. (3): a person authorised by an order must not import or deal with the waste "except in
-- accordance with the order".
-- s 26(1): a person must not export unless "(a) the person is the holder of an export permit ...; or (b) the export has been ordered
-- under any regulation made under Part 3" -- there is no limb for an export merely AUTHORISED by an order. (2): as s 25(2).
-- s 27(1): a person must not bring waste into Singapore in the course of a transit proposal "unless the person is the holder of a
-- transit permit" -- no order of either kind will do. (2): as s 25(2), including taking it out of Singapore.
-- s 12: "This Act does not apply to or in relation to any vessel or aircraft belonging to the naval, military or air forces of
-- Singapore or any other country."
DECLARE Shipment HAS
    `the kind of movement` IS A Movement
    `the goods are hazardous or other waste` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds the matching permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `kept to the permit and its conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised by an order under Part 3 regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `kept to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ordered under Part 3 regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on a naval or military vessel or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the shipment` IS A Shipment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shipment is an offence` IF
        (NOT `the shipment`'s `on a naval or military vessel or aircraft`)
    AND `the shipment`'s `the goods are hazardous or other waste`
    AND (IF `the shipment`'s `holds the matching permit`
         THEN NOT `the shipment`'s `kept to the permit and its conditions`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the shipment`'s `the kind of movement`
              WHEN `import` THEN
                    (`the shipment`'s `authorised by an order under Part 3 regulations` AND (NOT `the shipment`'s `kept to the order`))
                OR  ((NOT `the shipment`'s `authorised by an order under Part 3 regulations`) AND (NOT `the shipment`'s `ordered under Part 3 regulations`))
              WHEN `export` THEN NOT `the shipment`'s `ordered under Part 3 regulations`
              WHEN `transit` THEN TRUE)

-- ss 25(4), 26(3), 27(3): "(a) in the case of a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding $300,000; or (b) in the case of an individual,
-- to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both". A company faces three times the
-- fine but no imprisonment.
GIVEN `is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a shipment offence` MEANS
    IF `is a body corporate` THEN 300000 ELSE 100000

GIVEN `is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment for a shipment offence` MEANS
    IF `is a body corporate` THEN 0 ELSE 24

§§ `29, 30, 32 to 37 and 48 -- the enforcement offences`

-- Each is "liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both",
-- except ss 33(3) and 34(3), failing to produce a permit or order: "a fine not exceeding $3,000" and no imprisonment.
-- s 48(2)(e): regulations MAY create offences up to the same $10,000 or 12 months, with a further $1,000 a day for a continuing
-- offence; whether any regulation does is not known here.
DECLARE EnforcementOffence IS ONE OF
    `ignoring a notice to give information`
    `disobeying a requirement to move or hold a vessel, aircraft or vehicle`
    `refusing to answer or produce documents during a search`
    `failing to produce an import or export permit`
    `failing to produce a transit permit`
    `refusing reasonable assistance`
    `obstructing the Director-General or an officer`
    `making a false statement`
    `contravening regulations that create an offence`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN EnforcementOffence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to produce an import or export permit` THEN 3000
    WHEN `failing to produce a transit permit` THEN 3000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN EnforcementOffence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to produce an import or export permit` THEN 0
    WHEN `failing to produce a transit permit` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 12

-- Most of these offences are committed only "without reasonable excuse". The Act names two excuses: s 30(7), "if complying with the
-- requirement would have endangered the person or any other person"; s 32(4), refusing to answer or produce "if answering the
-- question, or producing the document, might tend to incriminate the person". It names none for s 29 (information notices) or
-- s 33 or s 34. This rule says only whether the Act NAMES the excuse; a court may still find an unnamed excuse reasonable.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN EnforcementOffence, `complying would endanger someone` IS A BOOLEAN, `it might incriminate the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act names a reasonable excuse` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disobeying a requirement to move or hold a vessel, aircraft or vehicle` THEN `complying would endanger someone`
    WHEN `refusing to answer or produce documents during a search` THEN `it might incriminate the person`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 37(1), (2): a person must not "knowingly or recklessly (a) make a statement that is false or misleading in a material particular;
-- or (b) give ... a document containing information that is false or misleading in a material particular without (i) indicating ...
-- that the document is false or misleading and in which respect it is so; and (ii) providing correct information ... if the person
-- has, or can reasonably obtain, the correct information".
GIVEN `knowingly or recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN, `false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is a document handed over` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `said it was false and where` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave the correct information or could not reasonably obtain it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a false statement offence` IF
        `knowingly or recklessly`
    AND `false or misleading in a material particular`
    AND ((NOT `it is a document handed over`) OR (NOT (`said it was false and where` AND `gave the correct information or could not reasonably obtain it`)))

§§ `31(2) -- entering a home`

-- s 31(2): the Director-General or an authorised officer "must not ... enter into any dwelling house in actual occupation, unless with
-- the consent of the occupier of the dwelling house or with 6 hours' previous notice to the occupier". (3): a court may by warrant
-- authorise entry, "if need be by force", where admission was refused or the place is unoccupied and the case is urgent.
-- INFERENCE: a warrant under (3) authorises entry to a dwelling despite (2).
GIVEN `an occupied dwelling house` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours of notice given` IS A NUMBER, `a court warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entry is permitted` IF
        (NOT `an occupied dwelling house`)
    OR  `the occupier consented`
    OR  `hours of notice given` AT LEAST 6
    OR  `a court warrant`

§§ `42 -- officers of a company`

-- s 42(1): where a body corporate commits an offence, a "director, manager, secretary or other similar officer", or one purporting to
-- act as such, "shall also be guilty of that offence ... unless the person proves that (a) the offence was committed without his or
-- her knowledge, consent or connivance; and (b) he or she had exercised all such diligence to prevent the commission of the offence".
-- (2): diligence is judged by regard to compliance assessments, an environmentally sound waste management system, contingency
-- procedures, and staff knowledge of the Act. Both limbs must be proved; the burden is the officer's.
GIVEN `the company committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `was a director, manager, secretary or similar officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no knowledge, consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the company committed an offence`
    AND `was a director, manager, secretary or similar officer`
    AND (NOT (`proved no knowledge, consent or connivance` AND `proved all due diligence`))

§§ `45 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 45: "Any applicant who is aggrieved by the refusal of the Director-General to grant a permit under this Act may, within 30 days of
-- the decision of the Director-General, appeal in writing to the Minister whose decision is final". Only a REFUSAL TO GRANT is
-- appealable under s 45; the Act gives no appeal against a permit condition or a revocation (the regulations may).
DECLARE PermitDecision IS ONE OF
    `a refusal to grant a permit`
    `a permit condition`
    `a revocation of a permit`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A PermitDecision, `days since the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister lies` IF
        `the decision` EQUALS `a refusal to grant a permit`
    AND `days since the decision` AT MOST 30
